&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager in the Internal Products and Technologies organization, you&#39;ll partner with Engineering, Design, Growth, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Support, and Finance to build the billing experiences every Claude customer uses, from the first purchase to the monthly invoice:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We own how customers buy and manage Claude: choosing and changing plans, viewing invoices, tracking usage and spend, and setting spend controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your work reaches everyone who pays for Claude: individuals upgrading a plan, teams adding seats, developers buying credits, and enterprise admins managing budgets across thousands of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll define how Claude should explain a charge, change a plan, or set a spend limit for a customer. You&#39;ll also define how admins set spend controls for the agents their teams run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll own billing experiences that convert well, resist abuse, and let customers resolve billing questions on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand customers across segments (consumers, developers, teams, and enterprise admins) and where billing friction costs us conversion, trust, or support volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Growth on purchase, upgrade, and plan-change flows, balancing conversion against clarity and long-term customer trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Trust &amp;amp; Safety to stop abuse of Claude plans and credits without adding friction for legitimate customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design agentic billing experiences: Claude answering billing questions, resolving common issues, and taking billing actions, with a confirmation step wherever a mistake would cost the customer money.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Design so every Claude product gives customers the same clear way to buy, upgrade, and manage spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product strategy and roadmap, synthesize competing stakeholder needs, and communicate prioritization clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 7+ years of product management experience, including self-serve purchase, subscription, or billing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have shipped self-serve experiences where you owned conversion and retention metrics and ran experiments to move them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong product design instincts, and can make a confusing concept like proration, overage, or credits clear on a single screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built LLM-powered or agentic product features, and have a point of view on when an agent should act on its own and when it should ask first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are equally credible discussing system design with engineers, abuse patterns with Trust &amp;amp; Safety, and funnels with Growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable making tradeoffs between growth, risk, and financial accuracy, and explaining them clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are scrappy and resourceful, and do what it takes to get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped customer tools for usage-based or hybrid pricing (seats, usage, credits), such as usage dashboards, spend limits, and alerts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked with Trust &amp;amp; Safety or risk teams to prevent abuse of plans, credits, or free trials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launched a product in new countries, including local pricing, tax, and currency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built self-serve help experiences that measurably reduced billing support contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled through hypergrowth (10x+ revenue).&lt;/li&gt;
