&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s Business Risk &amp;amp; Insurance (BRI) team, part of Treasury, safeguards the company&#39;s balance sheet, people and physical assets. We are the financial and operational safety net for a company building some of the world&#39;s most advanced AI systems, from large-scale compute and data center infrastructure to our offices and the products we put in customers&#39; hands. The team is scaling quickly as Anthropic grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Risk &amp;amp; Insurance Specialist, you&#39;ll build operational excellence across contracts, claims, and day-to-day insurance operations, using AI and automation to streamline processes wherever you can. You&#39;ll work closely with Compute, Engineering, Finance, Legal, Security, Product and Payroll to spot emerging risks early, help structure global insurance programs, support our risk-financing strategy and drive loss prevention. This is a rare chance to insure one of the fastest-growing companies, where parts of the risk landscape are still being defined, and to help Anthropic pursue its mission boldly by keeping our operations resilient and protected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insurance review of contracts: Review insurance and indemnity requirements in customer, vendor, lease, and compute agreements, and advise Legal and business partners on compliant, practical positions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insurance operations: Manage claims intake and tracking, certificates of insurance, broker coordination, and policy administration. Build a data warehouse / repository and repeatable processes as volume scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data gathering and reporting: Collect and maintain exposure data (property values, payroll, revenue, headcount, etc.) for renewals, audits, and underwriting submissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actuarial and quantitative analysis: Support limit-adequacy, loss, and retention analyses to inform program structure and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Captive operations: Support captive formation and ongoing operations, including fronting and reinsurance coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation: Identify and implement ways to automate manual insurance workflows using AI and workflow tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional support: Partner with Compute, Finance, Legal, and Payroll on insurance questions across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in insurance, corporate risk management, brokerage, underwriting, or risk consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience supporting a multi-line commercial insurance program (property, casualty, cyber/tech E&amp;amp;O, D&amp;amp;O/management liability, and similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–12 years in insurance, corporate risk management, brokerage, underwriting, or risk consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4 years on the corporate (buyer) side, or in a broker or carrier role serving corporate clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at, or insuring, a technology company or other fast-growing, complex organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Property insurance experience, including large or complex property, construction, or data center exposures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Captive insurance experience (formation, management, fronting, or reinsurance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience insuring emerging technology risks, such as AI or technology liability and cyber&lt;/li&gt;
