&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Salesforce Developer at Anthropic, you will design, build, and maintain the Salesforce platform that powers our core customer motions and quote-to-cash business.: This includes automation throughout the Salesforce platform ranging from core sales automation to product catalog and pricing, quoting and approvals, order and contract management, and the handoff to billing and provisioning. You&#39;ll work both autonomously and collaboratively across RevOps, Order Management, Legal, Billing Engineering, Deal Desk, Finance and Accounting, and Product to translate pricing and packaging requirements into scalable Apex, Flow, and integration solutions, and to extend our capabilities with custom code where necessary. We are an AI-first systems team, and you&#39;ll be expected to use Claude and our in-house AI development tooling as a core part of how you write, review, and ship code, always against our house standards for flexibility, maintainability, and scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you might sit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring across more than one team. Placement depends on your background and where you can have the most impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GTM Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Builds and runs the Salesforce platform and connected tools that Anthropic&#39;s sellers, sales leaders, and revenue operations teams rely on every day. You&#39;d build the automation behind how deals move through the pipeline, how leads and accounts reach the right owner, and how information flows between our sales tools and the rest of the business. You&#39;ll work directly with the analysts and operators who define the process, and see the impact on the people who use what you ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QTC Experiences:&lt;/strong&gt; A vertically integrated team that spans quoting through to provisioning agreements, as well as customer billing experiences over the term of their agreement. You&#39;d build the foundational systems for CPQ, order management, provisioning and billing experiences, envisioning how we make our sellers and ops teams orders of magnitude more efficient with Claude. You&#39;ll work cross-functionally with GTM, finance, accounting and other stakeholders. Your work will directly impact seller velocity and our GTM deal making capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Apex (triggers, services, selectors, batch/queueable), Lightning Web Components, and Flow automation following our house Apex standards and trigger framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build quote-to-cash infrastructure in Salesforce, including the product catalog and pricing data model, quote and order lifecycle, discount and approval automation, and amendment, renewal, and co-termination flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend CPQ and expand into agentic selling with custom pricing and quote-calculation logic, quote and order user experiences, and code built against the package&#39;s APIs and data model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own integrations between Salesforce and our billing, provisioning, and finance systems, such as Stripe, Metronome, and NetSuite, directly or via middleware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new product and pricing launches by modeling catalog, SKU, and pricing changes so they can be released quickly and reflected consistently in every downstream system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Claude and our internal AI development tooling as a first-class part of your build and code-review workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Business Systems analysts and Finance to ensure data-model decisions support downstream bookings, forecasting, and revenue reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with DevOps on release management for your work: sandbox strategy, source control, peer review, and deployment via SFDX/metadata tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure appropriate controls, test coverage, and documentation are in place for an effective control environment, particularly around pricing, discounting, and contract changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with ambiguity in a rapidly changing business, resolve problems independently, and propose solutions that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on Salesforce development experience (Apex, SOQL, LWC, Flow) in a production org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or extending CPQ and quote-to-cash functionality in Salesforce (Salesforce CPQ, Revenue Cloud, Nue, or similar): product and pricing data models, quote and order lifecycle, approval automation, and amendments and renewals, including custom code written against the CPQ package rather than configuration alone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Salesforce with billing, ERP, or provisioning systems via REST/Bulk APIs, middleware (Workato, Mulesoft, or similar), or direct callouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with SFDX, source-controlled metadata, and a sandbox-to-prod release process with peer review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active use of AI-assisted development tools (Claude, Copilot, Cursor, or similar) as part of how you write and review code, and the ability to speak to how you steer and verify their output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic SQL skills and comfort working alongside a data warehouse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication with sales, deal desk, finance and accounting, product, and engineering stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Platform Developer I and II certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Administrator or Application/System Architect certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Salesforce platform constraints: governor limits, bulkification, sharing and visibility, recursion control, and how they surface in CPQ-specific situations such as large quotes, calculation performance, and bulk amendments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing a CPQ solution end to end or re-platforming from one CPQ to another, not just maintaining an existing one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with billing and finance platforms such as Stripe, Metronome, or Oracle, and with usage-based or consumption pricing models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of how CPQ design decisions flow through to bookings, invoicing, and revenue recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience scaling Salesforce in a high-growth GTM environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
