&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Analyst, Travel &amp;amp; Expense, you will run the day-to-day financial controls, audit program, and executive reporting behind Anthropic&#39;s T&amp;amp;E function. T&amp;amp;E touches every employee, every legal entity, and every executive, and it runs on Navan, Brex, and negotiated supplier agreements. Spend and transaction volume have grown several-fold in the past six quarters, and the controls need to scale to meet a public-company standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Head of Travel &amp;amp; Expense in Finance Operations and work daily with Accounting, Tax, Payroll, Talent, Security, Legal, Finance Systems and Administrative Business Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls &amp;amp; SOX Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the day-to-day operation of key T&amp;amp;E controls, including approvals, card issuance and spend limits, segregation of duties, and policy exceptions, within the control framework set by the Head of T&amp;amp;E, who owns the overall T&amp;amp;E process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the T&amp;amp;E process narratives and risk and control matrix, and keep them current as systems and policies change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure correct GL coding and complete, accurate month-end reconciliations across Navan, Brex, and Workday, and support close, flux analysis, and accruals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the preparer for T&amp;amp;E controls and the day-to-day contact for internal and external auditors: gather and retain evidence, support walkthroughs and sample requests, and track remediation, escalating significant issues to the Head of T&amp;amp;E&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Expansion Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and maintain entity-level coding and approval flows in Brex and Navan as new legal entities and countries come online&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and operationalize country-specific rules for per diems, VAT reclaim, non-USD cards, receipt requirements, and local tax treatment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Tax, Payroll, and Global Mobility to ensure compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accurate intercompany treatment of T&amp;amp;E costs across entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T&amp;amp;E Audit Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design, build, and run a risk-based audit program covering sampling, anomaly detection, misuse escalation, and remediation tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor pre-spend rules, duplicate and split-transaction checks, and receipt and 30-day submission compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and reporting on policy compliance, exceptions, and control performance for Finance leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of T&amp;amp;E to deploy Claude to review transactions, flag policy exceptions, and automate recurring reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day T&amp;amp;E operations, supporting the growing volume of travel and expense activity and platform configuration and automation, so operations keep running without pulling focus from controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own transaction-level review and receipt follow-up, and help shape what should be automated rather than staffed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Benefits, Payroll and Legal to ensure the T&amp;amp;E program is compliant with relevant local and country requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in travel and expense, corporate accounting, internal audit, or finance operations, ideally at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on SOX or internal-controls experience: writing process narratives, testing or operating key controls, and working with external auditors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong accounting fundamentals, including GL coding, account reconciliations, accruals, and month-end close support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep platform expertise in Navan and/or comparable TMC platforms, plus Brex or equivalent expense management tools, and working knowledge of ERP integrations (Workday preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills: comfort with large transaction datasets, sampling methods, and anomaly detection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and discretion with sensitive information, and the ability to work credibly with senior executives and their support teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, with the ability to explain a control or an exception to Finance leaders, auditors, and employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-curious, builder mindset: experience automating finance workflows with AI tools, or real enthusiasm for doing so, and comfort creating structure where none exists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA, CIA, or equivalent certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-entity, multi-currency environments, including per diem rules, VAT reclaim, and cross-border tax considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pre-IPO or newly public company readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M&amp;amp;A integration experience a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
