&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Security Engineer to build the systems that triage and validate bug bounty and other externally reported security findings, not to work the queue, and this role suits a software engineer moving into security or a security engineer with a strong engineering background. You will build large language model (LLM) and agent-based tooling that validates findings, traces them to their root cause, and opens fixes for well-understood vulnerability classes. This is a hybrid role based in San Francisco or New York City, with three days a week in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the systems that take in externally reported vulnerabilities and assess validity, severity, and reproducibility at a volume manual triage cannot match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build LLM and agent-based analysis that validates business logic, authentication, and design-level findings, not just known signatures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build systems that trace validated findings to their root cause and propose, and increasingly open, fixes for well-understood vulnerability classes, with human review gates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the bug bounty program, including scope, policy, and researcher engagement, and feed every resolved report back into automated triage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the tooling into security testing capabilities that customers can use on what they build and deploy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering or security engineering experience, building and shipping production systems or internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wrote production code in JavaScript/TypeScript on Node.js, with hands-on experience in web frameworks such as Next.js or React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built with LLM or agent-based tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reproduced and assessed externally reported vulnerabilities, including judging severity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built security automation used across an engineering org, not just for your own team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built systems that auto-generate or propose code fixes, not just findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tested or secured multi-tenant platforms where customer-built applications run on shared infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
