&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Training and serving frontier AI models requires data center capacity at a scale and pace that conventional delivery models were not built for. Anthropic&#39;s Data Center Capacity Delivery team embeds with developers, general contractors, and third-party partners to take leased and partnered sites from deal close through floor access and operational handover as fast as they can safely be built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Reporting and Controls Lead, you&#39;ll own the single view of where every project in the delivery portfolio stands: consolidated milestone tracking from early floor access through floor access and ready-for-service, the integrity of the data behind it, and the capacity projections leadership plans against. You&#39;ll build and run the reporting the delivery team and executives rely on, and chase down the schedule and data discrepancies it surfaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly cross-functional role: you&#39;ll work with Senior Delivery Managers and Regional Managers in the field, our third-party project-management partners, and the planning, transaction, design, and deployment teams whose inputs and outputs the portfolio schedule depends on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MOC (Mission + Outcomes + Competencies)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Give the delivery team and leadership one trustworthy view of where every project stands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consolidated milestone tracking (early floor access, floor access, RFS) current across all projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schedule and status data reconciled at the source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Portfolio capacity projections and variance to plan maintained.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Delivery-review and executive reporting built; data-quality checks automated where possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Project controls / scheduling on large capital programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Portfolio-level, not single-job, reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scheduling, spreadsheet, and BI tooling fluency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identifying, qualifying, and packaging data driven insights that define project and portfolio health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own consolidated milestone tracking across all active and upcoming delivery projects — early floor access, floor access, ready for service — and keep it current&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Validate schedule and status data from developers, GCs, and third-party partners; challenge what doesn&#39;t reconcile and fix it at the source&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain portfolio capacity projections and the variance to plan behind them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain reporting for delivery reviews and executive updates&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define the data standards and integrated-schedule and tooling conventions projects report against, with the Program Management Lead&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Automate reporting and data-quality checks where possible, including with AI-assisted tools&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
